<p>Cost information needs the View internal Enom costs permission.</p>
<h2>Quote</h2>
<p>A quote is the renewal price read before anything is sent. A complete quote decides whether a sponsored renewal may be sent. A quote is never treated as the charge. An approval caps the accepted quote; Enom does not cap the final charge, which can differ.</p>
<h2>Confirmed charge</h2>
<p>A charge is confirmed only from the registrar order for that exact request: one line item for this domain and term, and an order total equal to that line amount. If the order total is missing or different, the charge stays unconfirmed. That holds even when the line amount or the quote shows a plausible price.</p>
<p>A change in the reseller balance alone never confirms a charge. Renewals sent with the expired-domain command have no accepted charge format, so their charge stays unconfirmed.</p>
<h2>Charge checks</h2>
<p>Charge evidence is read for completed registrations and renewals. While registrar reads are on, the worker checks unconfirmed charges at most once a day. Checks stop after 5 attempts. Check charge evidence on the domain page reads the order once more. It never resends the request.</p>
<h2>Over the limit</h2>
<p>If a confirmed charge is above the approved limit, automatic spending pauses for that domain until it is reviewed.</p>
